* mje15032.lib - onsemi MJE15032, NPN complementary silicon power
* transistor, TO-220, 250 V / 8.0 A / 50 W.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_npn/mje15032.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter Qmje15032
*
* NOTE THE MODEL NAME: it is Qmje15032, not MJE15032. The vendor named it
* that way and it was not "corrected" - see PROVENANCE below.
*
* Role in this project: the NPN half of the complementary Class A emitter
* follower that forms the output stage of the gain block
* (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:367). One instance per block.
*
* ADR-016 had written that if the two MJE lacked a manufacturer model the
* output stage would be a TOPOLOGY change, not a package swap. They do
* not lack one: this file is why the output stage stands.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_npn/mje15032.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE15032/PROVENANCE.json, and the reasoning in
* docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-10-L24-t7-dispositivi-attivi.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* onsemi serves this model as a .lib text file at
* /download/models/lib/mje15032.lib - the pattern L8 had not found, which
* is why Fase 1 had recorded only "models page exists, final file not
* confirmed". It was frozen byte-for-byte at
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE15032/mje15032.lib and copied here unchanged:
* nothing removed, no value rounded, reordered or "corrected", and the
* model NAME left as the vendor wrote it.
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE15032/mje15032.lib) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_npn/mje15032.lib)      # empty
*
* THE MODEL WAS WRITTEN BY A CONTRACTOR, AND THAT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN
* HIDDEN. Its own header says "Model Generated by MODPEX / Copyright(c)
* Symmetry Design Systems / Modeling services provided by Interface
* Technologies", generated 1 February 2004, PSpice format. A model the
* manufacturer DISTRIBUTES is what ADR-016 asks for; recording who
* authored it does not weaken the provenance, it is part of what
* provenance IS.
*
* Note the date: this model is 22 years old, and it is the newest thing
* onsemi publishes for the part.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - TWO POINTS ARE OUTSIDE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet MJE15032/D, frozen at
* vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/MJE15032/mje15032-d.pdf. ngspice 47, at the
* datasheet's own conditions, set temp = 25 (the datasheet is @ 25 C,
* ngspice defaults to 27, and XTB = 0.737 makes hFE temperature
* dependent):
*
*   hFE @ IC = 0.5 A, VCE = 5 V      66.389       70 MIN.     ***OUTSIDE***
*   hFE @ IC = 1.0 A, VCE = 5 V      61.335       50 MIN.     inside
*   hFE @ IC = 2.0 A, VCE = 5 V      53.488       10 MIN.     inside
*   fT  @ IC = 500 mA, VCE = 10 V,
*       ftest = 1.0 MHz              27.667 MHz   30 MHz MIN. ***OUTSIDE***
*
* THE hFE POINT MISSES THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN MINIMUM BY 5.1%. It is
* not a transcription error, because nothing was transcribed: the file is
* byte-for-byte as served. It is the manufacturer's model failing the
* manufacturer's datasheet, which is the same shape as NC-013 on the
* LSK489 and NC-020 on the LS352. Recorded as NC-024 in
* docs/preamp/NONCOMPLIANCE.md.
*
* WHICH DIRECTION IT ERRS, because that is what decides whether it is
* safe: the model has LESS gain than the part is guaranteed to have, so a
* figure computed with it is pessimistic on drive current and on the
* loading the driver sees. That is the safe direction - but it is not
* "conservative in a known amount", and the model does not describe a
* conforming part.
*
* THE fT POINT IS OUTSIDE TOO, AND THAT IS NEW IN L25 - it is NC-025.
* L24 recorded 31.04 MHz here and read it as inside. The number changes
* because of the DEFINITION, and the definition is the datasheet's own:
* Note 2 of MJE15032/D says "fT = hfe ftest", and the test row says
* ftest = 1.0 MHz. So fT is the gain-bandwidth product measured AT 1 MHz,
* not the |hfe| = 1 crossing. Measured at IC verified to 500.000 mA:
*
*   |hfe| at 1.0 MHz = 27.6667  ->  fT = 27.667 MHz, 7.8% BELOW the
*                                   30 MHz minimum
*   |hfe| = 1 crossing              30.713 MHz, which clears the minimum
*                                   by 2.4%
*
* The two disagree because at 1 MHz this device is only ~2.6 octaves
* above its own beta pole, so the roll-off is not yet the asymptote -
* which is true of the real part as well, and is exactly why the
* manufacturer specifies the test frequency. The comparison that means
* something is the one made the datasheet's way, and made that way the
* model does not reach the guaranteed minimum.
*
* Direction: the model is SLOWER than the guaranteed part, so phase and
* loop-gain figures computed with it are pessimistic - the safe
* direction, and the same shape as NC-020 on the LS352.
*
* THE 2.0 A POINT CORRECTS L24, which recorded it as "not reached". That
* was an artefact of how far its base sweep went, not a property of the
* model: swept to Vb = 1.6 V the model reaches IC = 6.8 A smoothly and
* monotonically, and 2.0 A - where the datasheet asks for 10 minimum -
* comes out at 53.5.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE NUMBERS THE DATASHEET DOES NOT GIVE, AND THEY MATTER MORE HERE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* The datasheet specifies hFE at 0.5 / 1.0 / 2.0 A. THE PROJECT RUNS THIS
* DEVICE AT 14.71 mA (gain_block.py:434) - 34 times below the lowest
* specified point, where the datasheet says nothing and only the model
* speaks. It says:
*
*   hFE @ 15 mA      75.73        (re-measured in L25)
*   fT  @ 15 mA      11.24 MHz    (L24's figure, NOT re-measured here)
*
* Two things follow. The fT at the working point is far lower than at the
* test point, and the hand-written placeholder used the test-point figure
* - that is the "2.8x fast" row of ADR-017. And hFE 75.7 here
* against 129.4 for the PNP MJE15033 is a 1.7x IMBALANCE inside a
* complementary follower, which the placeholders could not show because
* they were symmetric by construction (BF = 100 on both). Fase 4
* material.
*
* At the datasheet's own test point, measured the datasheet's own way,
* this device does not clear its fT minimum at all - see NC-025 above.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT THIS MODEL DOES NOT HAVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE. The line carries KF=0 and AF=1 explicitly, which is
* the same thing as having none: the flicker term is multiplied by KF.
* In this repo only models/jfet/lsk489.lib has 1/f noise (NC-004).
*
* No SPICE magnitude suffix appears in the model line, so
* docs/limitations.md #13 has nothing to bite on here.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* BELOW THIS LINE: THE VENDOR FILE, BYTE FOR BYTE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
